# BD follow-up draft pack (2026-07-30): per-job override for agent_propose.sh
# (AGENT_JOB_OVERRIDES). Non-secret task wiring only — API keys stay in the canonical
# secrets.env, sourced first.
#
# EXAMPLE ONLY. The live file lives OUTSIDE git at
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/bd_followup_drafts.env  (mode 600, owned by dave)
# and is intentionally NOT committed — mirrors knowledge_digest.env exactly.
# Install: install -m 600 profiles/bd_followup_drafts.env.example \
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/bd_followup_drafts.env
#
# Why this exists: bd-stall-radar flags stalled deals and stops at flagging. This job
# writes the text — up to five copy-paste-ready drafts for every Dave-owed BD next action
# (radar stalls + Client Pipeline rows past their Next action date + due BD Task Inbox
# rows). Runs headless Claude Code (Opus 5, box subscription, $0 OpenRouter spend) and
# refuses to run at all (bin/vault_sync_guard.sh check) rather than draft off a stale
# mirror — a draft built on stale facts leaves the box for a real client.
AGENT_PROFILE=claude-opus
# AGENT_OWNER names the owning persona (design/agents/<owner>.toml) — the owner= field of the run
# log. Until T6.1 (2026-09-16) it also keyed a Hermes episodic store under ~/.hermes/profiles; that
# store is retired and nothing on this runtime reads or writes one. AGENT_PROFILE still names the
# RUNTIME and keys cost.log's profile= column (W1, 2026-09-02).
AGENT_OWNER=claudius
AGENT_TASK_SLUG=bd-followup-drafts
# Time budget — bin/propose_budget.py; tests/test_propose_budget.sh pins it under the unit's
# TimeoutStartSec. Per attempt: 1.5 x the longest measured success (910s, cost.log to
# 2026-10-06), up to 5 min, floor 10. Only a failure inside AGENT_RETRY_WITHIN_SECONDS is retried.
AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
AGENT_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=25
AGENT_RETRY_BASE_SECONDS=30
AGENT_RETRY_WITHIN_SECONDS=300
AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/run_bd_followup_drafts_cc.sh'
AGENT_VERIFY_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/proposal_or_decline.sh bd-followup-drafts'
